Z||000005||Raydar||10-22-2000||05:45 PM||||FD...<BR>Regarding the wrap around spoiler, I've seen two different designs for this same item.<BR>IRM's wrap-around spoiler was around $185. The tail edge of it goes all the way to the bottom edge of the trunk lid. I bought one a couple of years ago, but was not real happy with the quality. Was warped, and the hole that is drilled for access to the lock cylinder is very deep, as the piece is 3/4" thick, in that area. Had to bevel the hole out, to leave room to get my key in to unlock the trunk.<BR>RS Motorsports also sells one. $220, US. The tail edge of this one comes down to about the center of the lock cylinder.  <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/wrap.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/wrap.jpg</A> <BR>Strangely enough, the <I>first</I> spoiler of this type that I bought in 86 from DGP, who sold out to IRM, was of this design.<BR>If I buy another one, I'm gonna go with RSM's.<BR>Their homepage is at: <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/</A> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-22-2000).]||||reg||1
